Z||000000||winddancer||11-12-2000||11:13 PM||||my prob is when i got off the freeway my shifter had no responce when i tried to take off it felt like i was taking off in 4th and then it locked up it wont go forward but it will go backwards can someone help me please e-mail me at ksisco@evansinet.com <BR>i have a 85 fiero <BR>i also can move the shifter seltor at the tranny with no resistance if this will help<BR>i have had the car runing and tried to go forward @ 3-4000 rpm and it will just kill the engine but i can push it backwards if someone can help i apereciate it it is a 4 speed manual <BR>                       thank you<P>[This message has been edited by winddancer (edited 11-12-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by winddancer (edited 11-13-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by winddancer (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||StuGood||11-13-2000||06:27 PM||||Sounds like your shifter is no longer connected to the tranny.  Think (?) at this point, it's stuck in "Park."<P>Check the cable ends, on top of the tranny, and in the console.  When you move the selector, the lever on top of the tranny should move.  Have someone watch the tranny lever while someone else moves the selector.  If the tranny lever isn't moving, either the cable's busted or one of the ends came loose.   ||||reg||9
Z||000002||winddancer||11-13-2000||06:35 PM||||i am sorry i think i forgot to metion that it is a four speed and when i move the shift seltor at the tranny it moves the shifter and there is no restance and it wont move forward but i can push it backwards ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-13-2000||06:51 PM||||You <B>did</B> say it was a 4-speed.  Apparently, I just can't read.  The word "selector" just threw me.  My bad...<P>Change my previous guess to,"Sounds like it's stuck halfway into 4th gear."<P>Anyway, it kind of sounds like one of the the nuts holding the cable ends to the lever (at the trans.) might have gotten loose, and the cable end slipped in its slot.  So now it's out of adjustment.  Loosen the nut so the lever can move independent of the cable end.  The lever should click into 3 positions.  Click it into the middle (neutral) position.  Move the shifter (in the car) to about the middle.  Tighten the cable nut (at the trans).<P>Now get into the car and check to see if it  can shift into all the gears.  If you don't like it, loosen the cable nut again and make minor adjustments as required.<P>It could be the cable broke, or internal problems in the trans, but those're harder to fix, so we'll not talk about that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">       ||||reg||7
Z||000004||theogre||11-13-2000||06:52 PM||||Take the linkage off the tranny and see if you can get it into gears with the levers on the tranny.<P>You can push it backwards but not forward? That could be bad. may indicate soemthing is laying in a set of gears. It lets the gears turn one way but jams them in the other direction. If you don't have any luck with the levers then you may have to rip it apart. (If you can't change to all gears with the levers it a bad sign. several things can cause that, all of them mean opening the tranny.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||winddancer||11-13-2000||06:54 PM||||thank you i will try that||||reg||10
Z||000006||winddancer||11-13-2000||07:10 PM||||i tried what you said but its is like the shift fork is not selecting any gears it moves freely like there is no gears <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000007||Oreif||11-13-2000||07:30 PM||||The shifting fork is broken or bent. Happened to a friends 86. You cannot find new parts for the 4spd. You can get a used one or convert it over to a 5spd. (He opted for swapping in a getreg 5spd)||||reg||1
